[{"text":"GSE[p] can be used as input for a D-4-dimensional \\gamma \\cdot p = \\gamma^\\mu p_\\mu and is transformed into DiracGamma[Momentum[p,D-4],D-4] by FeynCalcInternal (FCI). GSE[p,q, ...] is a short form for GSE[p].GSE[q]. ....","anchor":"gse"},{"text":"Overview, DiracGamma, GA, GAD, GSD.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"GSE[p]","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{p}\\]","anchor":"cb1-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GSE[p] // FCI // StandardForm (*DiracGamma[Momentum[p, -4 + D], -4 + D]*)","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GSE[p, q, r, s]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{p}\\right).\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{q}\\right).\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{r}\\right).\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{s}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb3-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GSE[p, q, r, s] // StandardForm (*GSE[p] . GSE[q] . GSE[r] . GSE[s]*)","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"GSE[q] . (GSE[p] + m) . GSE[q]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{q}\\right).\\left(m+\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{p}\\right).\\left(\\hat{\\gamma }\\cdot \\hat{q}\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"In order to use Dirac algebra with D-4 dimensional objects you need to activate the t’Hooft-Veltman-Breitenlohner-Maison scheme first","anchor":"cb5-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"]; DiracSimplify[GSE[q] . GS[q] . GSE[q]]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{\\$Aborted}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"BMHV\"]; DiracSimplify[GSE[q] . GS[q] . GSE[q]]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\hat{q}^2 \\left(-\\left(\\bar{\\gamma }\\cdot \\overline{q}\\right)\\right)\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCSetDiracGammaScheme[\"NDR\"];","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"}]